   "default": true,
   "notes": "Equations 1-6 define a 300 K third-order Birch-Murnaghan reference isotherm plus relative Mie-Gruneisen-Debye thermal pressure: gamma=gamma0(V/V0)^q and theta=theta0 exp[(gamma0-gamma)/q], with n=2 atoms per formula unit. K0T=160 GPa and theta0=500 K were fixed; V0, K0T', gamma0, and q were fitted in stages. The source does not state a confidence convention for parenthetical errors or publish coefficient covariance. All 34 observations are bundled; only the 23 rows below 47 GPa belong to the published high-spin fit. The stored parameterization gives 0.1233 GPa pressure RMSE across those rows and reproduces the paper's printed calculated pressures within 0.014 GPa. An independent unweighted staged refit gives V0=75.80705 A^3 and K0'=4.13454 at 300 K, then gamma0=1.52863 and q=0.68230 using the published cold curve; thermal-parameter parity is achieved, while the room-temperature coefficient difference is retained because the paper does not specify weights or objective details.",
